<title>CHINA: China forecasts 1997 sorghum output 5.5 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>China forecasts 1997 sorghum output 5.5 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>China estimated total sorghum output this year at about 5.5 million tonnes, compared with a total of 5.68 million tonnes in 1996, an official of the State Statistical Bureau said on Monday.</p>
<p>The bureau said the area planted with sorghum reached a total of 1.23 million hectares this year, down by 50,000 hectares from 1996, he said by telephone.</p>
<p>&quot;The soaring consumption by the distilling industry has pushed up consumption of sorghum and the total consumption of sorghum in 1996 was estimated to be close to six million tonnes,&quot; the official said by telephone.</p>
<p>The price was expected to rise because of the gap between supply and demand, he said, but gave no more details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
